<div style="padding-left: 30px;"><hr />Lake Tahoe Community College uses Canvas as the learning management system to deliver online courses to students. Before you teach an online course you must be certified to use Canvas.</div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;">&nbsp;</div>
<div>
<table class="ou-chevron-list"><caption>Chevron List</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Add bulleted list here</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>
<ul>
<li><span style="font-size: 18pt;">Online Faculty Handbook</span></li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;"><hr />Once you are certified to use Canvas you will be added to the Online Faculty Handbook. In the handbook you will be able to decide if online teaching is right for you, and:</div>
<div style="padding-left: 60px;"><span>&bull; your responsibilities as an online instructor</span></div>
<div style="padding-left: 60px;"><span><span>&bull; important components to add to your Canvas course</span></span></div>
<div style="padding-left: 60px;"><span>&bull; what actions you need to take before, during, and after the quarter</span></div>
<div style="padding-left: 60px;"><span><span>&bull; resources to enhance your courses</span></span></div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;"><span><span>The Online Faculty Handbook is a Canvas site that you will be able to access once you log into Canvas.</span></span></div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;">&nbsp;</div>
<div style="padding-left: 30px;"><span><span>If you are new and don't have access to Canvas please contact us.</span></span></div>
<div>&nbsp;</div>
</td>
<td>
